  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nRisk-off Friday with futures bleeding red ahead of jobs data. SPY down 1.5% to $745, but tech getting hammered with QQQ off nearly 3% and XLK down over 4%. VIX spiking to 24.68 signals real fear, while defensive sectors like staples and utilities are catching bids.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Non-Farm Payrolls (12:30 ET)</strong> - The big kahuna. Market's pricing in volatility with VIX elevated. Any surprise could amplify today's moves.</li>\n<li><strong>Middle East Tensions</strong> - Iran firing warning missiles at US warships in Gulf of Oman. Geopolitical risk premium building in energy and defense names.</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Breakdown</strong> - XLK down 4.35% pre-market. Watch if this is sector rotation or broader risk-off that spreads.</li>\n<li><strong>Boeing (BA) Production News</strong> - 737 Max new assembly line starting July 6. Industrial play in focus.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Tech leading the selloff with growth names getting crushed. If jobs data disappoints or geopolitical tensions escalate, we could see a full risk-off cascade into the weekend.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClassic flight to quality underway. Consumer staples (XLP) up 1.85%, utilities gaining, and healthcare holding strong while tech gets annihilated. This isn't just profit-taking - it's defensive positioning ahead of weekend geopolitical uncertainty. Energy down despite Middle East headlines, suggesting broader risk-off trumps sector-specific catalysts.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Jobs data at 12:30 ET is the make-or-break moment. With tech already weak and VIX elevated, any deviation from expectations could trigger major moves in either direction.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY $740</strong> - Key support. Break below opens door to $725 gap fill from May.</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ $715</strong> - Critical level holding pre-market. Lose this and $700 comes into play fast.</li>\n<li><strong>VIX $25</strong> - Above this level and we're in legitimate fear territory. Watch for acceleration.</li>\n<li><strong>XLK $210</strong> - Tech ETF at make-or-break level. Sector leadership hangs in the balance.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
